<Base title="Impact & Transparency" description="GEAR Moto Foundation's approach to accountability, outcome reporting and transparent program development.">
<section class="inner-hero"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">Accountability</div><h1>Trust Is Built<br/><span class="accent">Through Action.</span></h1></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="wrap prose"><h2>Our Transparency Commitment</h2><p>As the foundation develops, our intention is to publish meaningful program results, report stewardship of contributed funds, maintain objective grant policies, and explain how community support advances the mission.</p><p>We will distinguish verified accomplishments from goals and projections. At present, there are no published operating grant results to report.</p><h2>What We Plan to Measure</h2><ul><li><strong>Gear:</strong> Riders equipped and safety equipment distributed.</li><li><strong>Education:</strong> Training awards, course completions, and endorsements achieved where voluntarily reported.</li><li><strong>Assistance:</strong> Resource connections, referral categories, and riders or households helped with navigation.</li><li><strong>Recovery:</strong> Qualifying medical and hardship awards, verified expenses relieved, and people supported during recovery.</li><li><strong>Operations:</strong> Event activity, donors, sponsors, volunteer participation, and financial stewardship.</li></ul><h2>Governance &amp; Privacy</h2><p>The proposed governance model uses independent board oversight, documented conflicts and recusals, objective program eligibility, appropriate financial controls, and restricted access to beneficiary records. Recipients will not be required to share personal stories publicly.</p><div class="program-callout"><strong>Formation and filings:</strong> Draft bylaws, plans and five-year forecasts are not evidence of incorporation, IRS recognition, adopted policies, or actual financial performance. Official documents will be published when finalized and approved.</div><a href="/contact/">Ask a transparency question →</a></div></section></Base>